# Knowledge Vault

Open [START-HERE.md](START-HERE.md) in Obsidian or point an agent at [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).
This is a working vault, not the [core engineering checkout](https://github.com/bitpantry/knowledge-management).

## What belongs here

`catalog/` records sources and where to find them. `knowledge/` contains concepts, evidence,
decisions and interpretations. `extensions/` starts empty apart from its README;
add a domain extension only when you need one. Keep originals in their source systems.
If using Git, track approved records and extensions. Do not commit credentials,
raw source material, staging files, or anything the repository audience is not authorized to see.
A private repository does not authorize sharing client material.

## Update the core

From the vault folder, preview the latest published release from the eng base:

```sh
python3 -B core/update.py
python3 -B core/update.py --apply --commit FULL_COMMIT_FROM_PREVIEW
```

Preview does not write to the vault. Apply updates only verified shared files:
`core/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, and the bundled source-recovery example.
The installed revision and file fingerprints live in `.core-release.json`;
track that file if the vault uses Git. Local changes to shared files block
the update rather than being overwritten. Keep live records, installed
extensions, settings, `README.md`, and `START-HERE.md` as they are. A public
release needs no GitHub sign-in; private access uses an authenticated GitHub CLI.

Run the checks below and review the diff before committing. Do not run the
updater concurrently with other edits or Git operations. If an update was
interrupted, compare with a known good checkout before retrying. Release assets
on this channel are for compatible core updates only; any data migration needs
separate review and testing.

```sh
python3 -B core/catalog.py check
python3 -B core/concepts.py check
python3 -B core/reconcile_extension.py check
```
